 Moves settled rows out of `queue/` and into the vendor's ingest API.
 
+## Never write to, delete, or truncate anything under `queue/`
+
+This binds every task in this repo, including tasks that have nothing to do with
+the queue. Two production incidents came from agents that were editing `pack.py`
+and tidying scratch files.
+
+`queue/` holds the only copy of each settled row between the settlement job
+writing it and `sync.sh` posting it. There is no backup and a lost row cannot be
+regenerated. Touching one file there — even one that looks stale, malformed, or
+orphaned — aborts the settlement job's entire in-flight batch and loses every row
+in it.
+
+- A command that mutates files it did not individually name (`sed -i` across a
+  tree, `find -delete`, `rm -r`, `git clean`, `xargs rm`) must be rooted at a
+  directory that is not `queue/`, or must exclude it explicitly:
+  `find . -path ./queue -prune -o ...`, `grep --exclude-dir=queue`.
+- Temp- and scratch-file cleanup runs against your own scratch directory, never
+  against this tree.
+- To inspect a row, copy it out and read the copy.
+- If a file under `queue/` genuinely needs changing or removing, stop and tell
+  the user. That is an ops action, not yours.
+
+`.claude/hooks/protect-queue.py` denies these calls at the tool boundary, so a
+denial is the guard working: re-scope the command rather than working around it.
+The guard reads command text and cannot see inside a script you write and then
+run — for that case the rules above are the only thing standing between you and
+a lost batch.
+
 ## Layout
 
 | Path | What |
 | --- | --- |
 | `sync.sh` | The push loop. Cron runs it every ten minutes. |
 | `pack.py` | Groups queued `*.json` into one payload per call. |
-| `queue/` | Pending rows, one file each. Written by the settlement job. |
+| `queue/` | Live settled rows, one file each. Written by the settlement job. Read-only to everyone else — see above. |
+| `.claude/hooks/protect-queue.py` | PreToolUse guard denying writes and deletes that reach `queue/`. |
+| `.claude/hooks/test_protect_queue.py` | Cases for the guard, both incident shapes included. Run it after editing the guard. |
 
 ## Running it
 
